<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zawar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zawar is a mining area about 40 km south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> and one of the oldest known centres of zinc production in the world. Mining there goes back more than two thousand years, and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> its smelters were distilling metallic zinc in clay retorts on a large scale, centuries before the process was known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The mines continued under the maharanas of Mewar and are still worked today.</p></div>
